{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"593ec009e6bba4b34857c98825b17f1914ecd82c70fa05299065f4c0703d4ad9","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_c3e4aeb4f28fc722505d9c2d6d6b7bffe2f2c4f3ae8fdb8f9b4bee412ad98ab1","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a methodological contribution to multi-view representation learning. The supplied text does not contain a broader impact statement, ethics discussion, or specific compliance documentation. The use of the XRMB speech corpus involves human subjects, but the paper does not explicitly detail consent or IRB approval within the provided text. The paper is not anonymized, displaying author names and affiliations, which is consistent with the venue metadata (ICLR 2017) but precludes a double-blind compliance assessment without a specific policy anchor. No evidence of plagiarism or dual submission is present in the text.","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","paper_identity_sha256":"fb47a0828198610131e6e842826ca1d813148ffd75a7a5b0898cf094120ca8c4","prompt_identity_sha256":"caa34f1559c798efbbd5e7af6382c33abf5526d8940f086194bd4c201e80160f","raw_response_sha256":"cf2c6275e604278ed01d80ca5874e3965c60538c57f78228298e25b0c1025a16","request_identity_sha256":"f2392c39932d6803a04535d63b5a9a19bffb48b335375c4cbf99d010c86151f1","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"b821e43be712e80f9ef8a1c1bd694e1cef6c4afedb10f9131936b7e1cfdffab5","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section on ethics, responsible AI, or potential harms. The proposed method, Deep Variational Canonical Correlation Analysis, is a representation learning technique applied to standard datasets (MNIST, XRMB, MIR-Flickr). No specific ethical risks, such as bias, fairness, or dual-use concerns, are discussed or mitigated in the text. The absence of such discussion is noted, but no material ethical risk pathway is explicitly supported by the paper's content.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the Wisconsin X-ray microbeam (XRMB) corpus, which contains speech and articulatory measurements from 47 American English speakers. The text describes the data split and preprocessing (removing per-speaker mean and variance) but does not explicitly state whether informed consent was obtained from the participants or if the data usage complies with specific privacy regulations or licensing terms. The other datasets (MNIST, MIR-Flickr) are standard public benchmarks, but no specific licensing or consent documentation is provided in the paper text.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors (Weiran Wang, Xinchen Yan, Honglak Lee, Karen Livescu) and their institutional affiliations (TTI-Chicago, University of Michigan) on the first page. It also provides email addresses. This format is not anonymized. However, the metadata indicates the venue is ICLR 2017. Without a frozen policy anchor confirming that ICLR 2017 enforced double-blind review, this cannot be declared a policy violation. It is noted that the submission is not anonymized.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied paper text does not contain any explicit disclosure of plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. There is no evidence of textual or figure overlap with other works, nor any statement indicating simultaneous submission to other venues. The absence of such evidence in the text is insufficient to prove originality or the absence of dual submission, but no specific violation is observable in the provided material.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics a